<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Buea</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Buea is a town on the eastern slopes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-cameroon">Mount Cameroon</a> and the capital of the Southwest Region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a>. Its cool climate led the Germans to make it the seat of government of Kamerun from 1901 to 1909. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> it became the centre of the British-ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-cameroons">Southern Cameroons</a>, which joined Cameroon in 1961.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/buea.jpg" alt="Buea" width="320" height="166" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buea_from_Fako.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
